{
  "slug": "supreme-court-drafting",
  "name": "Supreme Court Drafting",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "For every advocate-on-record and senior counsel who files before the Supreme Court of India — and every junior who drafts under one — this is an open-source Claude Code plugin that takes a case folder (facts, pleadings, statutory anchor, prayer brief) and walks it through a six-agent pipeline (Reader → Format → Drafter → Verifier → Refiner → Overseer) the way a Supreme Court chamber actually works. Covers Special Leave Petitions (Civil and Criminal), Article 32 Writ Petitions, Transfer Petitions, Review Petitions, and Curative Petitions, with the Supreme Court Rules 2013 (Orders XXI, XXII, XL, XLVIII), Articles 32 / 136 / 137 / 142, the Rupa Ashok Hurra discipline, and the Supreme Court Registry Practice Directions baked into the Verifier. The finished product is a Registry-ready pleading the team can paginate, sign, and file at the Supreme Court Registry the same working day.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **8 skills** and **6 agents**.\n\n- **Skills** (8): `_drafting_common` (Shared reference for all Supreme Court of India drafting skills), `_sc_pleading_base` (Universal pleading skeleton for the Supreme Court of India), `curative-petition-draft` (Draft a Curative Petition before the Supreme Court of India under the jurisprudence laid down in Rupa Ashok…), `review-petition-draft` (Draft a Review Petition before the Supreme Court of India under Article 137 of the Constitution read with…), `slp-civil-draft` (Draft a Special Leave Petition (Civil) before the Supreme Court of India under Article 136 of the Constitution…), `slp-criminal-draft` (Draft a Special Leave Petition (Criminal) before the Supreme Court of India under Article 136 of the Constitution…), `transfer-petition-draft` (Draft a Transfer Petition before the Supreme Court of India under Section 25 of the Code of Civil…), `writ-art32-draft` (Draft a Writ Petition before the Supreme Court of India under Article 32 of the Constitution read with…)\n- **Agents** (6): `drafter` (Third agent in SC drafting pipeline), `format` (Second agent in SC drafting pipeline), `overseer` (Sixth and final agent in SC drafting pipeline), `reader` (First agent in SC drafting pipeline), `refiner` (Fifth agent in SC drafting pipeline), `verifier` (Fourth agent in SC drafting pipeline)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install supreme-court-drafting@claude-community` from `Wolfgangrush/supreme-court-drafting-litigation`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot"
  ],
